{# ============================================================================
   WATCHES — the four columns the roster owns on a station, ported from the
   design's configure.html#watches.

   THE NAME, KIND, POINT AND CALL SIGN ARE THE AREA'S. This section edits only
   what the roster owns: the shifts a post expects, how long its silence may
   run, how long before that is offline, and how wide its catchment is. Ruled
   18 sep, and it is why the rows here are read-only about everything else.

   ONE PLACE IT IS EDITED, TWO DOORS ONTO IT. The same block renders on the
   area's own Stations configure card; both call StationWatchService, and
   neither screen owns the other.

   A POST WITH NO WATCH IS NOT A FAULT. A post that declares none is never
   counted, never late and never a hole — only offline. The posts the area
   registers that are not on these books are named at the foot rather than
   silently missing.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{% block roster_section %}
<form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <div class="c rband">
        <div class="rb-hd">
            <span class="tab">Watches</span>
            <span class="rb-ttl">what each post expects, how long its silence may run, and how wide its catchment is</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rb-body">
            {% for watch in watches %}
                {% set station = watch.station %}
                {% set id = station.id %}
                <div class="rset">
                    <span class="lb"><b>{{ station.name }}</b><em>{{ station.code ?: '—' }}</em></span>
                    <span class="ct">
                        {% for shift in shifts %}
                            <label class="r-sh {{ shift.key in watch.expects ? 'on' : '' }}">
                                <input type="checkbox" name="expects_{{ id }}[]" value="{{ shift.key }}"
                                       {{ shift.key in watch.expects ? 'checked' : '' }}
                                       {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                                <i></i>{{ shift.label|lower }}
                            </label>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="r-sh">no shift vocabulary</span>
                        {% endfor %}
                        {% if watch.expectsNothing %}<span class="r-sh">no watch</span>{% endif %}
                    </span>
                    <span class="why">
                        <span class="unit">silence</span>
                        <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="silence_{{ id }}" value="{{ watch.silenceWindowMinutes }}" aria-label="Silence window for {{ station.name }}, minutes" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="unit">min, offline after</span>
                        <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="offline_{{ id }}" value="{{ watch.offlineAfterMinutes }}" aria-label="Offline threshold for {{ station.name }}, minutes" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="unit">min, catchment</span>
                        <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="catchment_{{ id }}" value="{{ watch.catchmentMetres }}" aria-label="Catchment for {{ station.name }}, metres" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="unit">m</span>
                        <span class="unit">pool {{ pools[id]|default(0) }}</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% else %}
                <div class="rfrag"><b>No post is on the roster&rsquo;s books yet</b><em>the area registers {{ band.stationsInArea }} station{{ band.stationsInArea == 1 ? '' : 's' }}; a watch is given to a post deliberately, so none is assumed</em></div>
            {% endfor %}
            <div class="rfrag"><b>The name, kind, point and call sign are the AREA&rsquo;s</b><em>this section edits only the four columns the roster owns, and it is the same block the area&rsquo;s Stations configure card renders</em></div>
            <div class="rfrag"><b>A post with no watch is not a fault</b><em>a post that declares none is never counted, never late and never a hole &mdash; only offline</em></div>
        </div>
        <div class="rb-foot">
            <span class="k">{{ postsOffTheBooks|length }} of the area&rsquo;s posts declare no watch and are not listed</span>
            <span class="sp"></span>
            {% if mayManage %}<button type="submit" class="cta">Save the watches</button>{% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>
{% endblock %}
